#                                          -1, -2 ... exactly as github-slugger does
# Slugs follow github-slugger (vendor/github-slugger): lower-case, delete what its
# regex deletes, each space becomes "-", over the text GitHub renders (links keep
# their text, tags and entities go, _emphasis_ pairs are removed, `code` is
# literal). Its two Unicode tables are generated below. A heading with no
# rendered text gets no anchor, as on GitHub.
# Not anchors: YAML front matter; fenced code; `code spans`; HTML comments; a
# heading inside an HTML block (CommonMark types 1, 6, 7); a backslash-escaped
# \<a; an <a id> on a line indented four spaces or a tab.
# Measured 2026-09-24 against GitHub's own rendering: 2,117 of 2,117 anchors
